.TH "FWD SEND" "1" "2026-08-12" "fwdit" "fwd send Manual"
.SH NAME
fwd\-send \- Start, follow, background, list, or cancel durable remote tasks.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fwd send
[OPTIONS] [arguments]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Start, follow, background, list, or cancel durable remote tasks.
.PP
Every command and agent turn runs in remote tmux and receives a task id.
During streams, Ctrl-C cancels and Ctrl-B
backgrounds. Add --stop-after to stop compute remotely when new work
finishes; 'fwd send stopafter'
queues it after current work and 'fwd send cancel stopafter' cancels it.
Reattach with
\&'fwd send TASK_ID', cancel queued work with 'fwd send cancel
[TASK_ID|all]', and list with
\&'fwd send --ls'. Never starts or restarts compute. Use '--' before raw
commands:
fwd send -- python train.py --epochs 10
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n,\fP \-\-name <str>
Session name, target, or backend; defaults to this directory's session.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fP <float>
Cancel the remote task if it exceeds this many seconds.
.TP
\fB\-d,\fP \-\-detach
Start the task in the background and return immediately.
.TP
\fB\-\-wait\fP
Stream until completion; this is the default unless --detach is passed.
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\fP
Cancel the selected task; with an agent message, cancel the active turn
and send the replacement.
.TP
\fB\-\-immediate\fP
Agent shorthand for --stop MESSAGE: cancel the active turn and
immediately send this message.
.TP
\fB\-\-stop\-after\fP
Queue a remote-owned stop action after the new command or agent turn finishes.
.TP
\fB\-\-force\fP
With --stop-after or 'stopafter', permit shutdown even if the remote Git
worktree is dirty.
.TP
\fB\-\-ls\fP
List send tasks instead of starting one.
.TP
\fB\-\-all\fP
With --ls, include completed, failed, and canceled tasks.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fP <auto|rich|markdown|json>
With --ls, choose Rich, Markdown, or JSON output.  [default: auto]
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fP
Render structured output as JSON; shorthand for --format json.
.SH EXIT STATUS
For a foreground command, fwd returns the remote command's exit status.
Other nonzero values indicate selection, transport, task-control, or
validation failure.
.SH REPORTING BUGS
Report issues at \fIhttps://github.com/Sid-MB/fwd/issues\fP.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBfwd\fP(1)
